+# v38 — BlueStacks ADB background mode
+
+ADB is now the default input mode for Gem Sniper and Gem Spy. Android screenshots
+and a persistent Android touch session replace desktop screenshots/mouse input.
+The Windows mouse and foreground window stay untouched. Mouse mode is still an
+explicit option in Settings and never serves as an automatic fallback.
+
+1. Enable Android Debug Bridge in BlueStacks Settings → Advanced. Keep the
+   selected device at `127.0.0.1:5555` unless your BlueStacks reports another port.
+2. Open the large Loong Haven map. In Gem Sniper → Settings, use **Test connection /
+   preview** while BlueStacks is visible. This can align Android pixels with your
+   existing routes using a read-only window capture.
+3. Minimize BlueStacks and use **Test map pan (minimized)**. It moves the camera
+   slightly and restores it. It never clicks a gem or walks your character.
+4. Save, then start Sniper or Spy. Keep the game active inside Android.
+
+BlueStacks must remain running and continue rendering while minimized. The pan
+test diagnoses paused rendering; a failed test does not claim background support.
+Resolution changes, black/corrupt screenshots, known app switches and transport
+failures stop ADB input while preserving progress. F10 cancels active commands,
+releases the Android finger and stays stopped. A helper watchdog releases a held
+touch after loss of heartbeat. Unknown Android focus metadata is accepted when
+the large game map is visually confirmed; a null focus is not treated as failure.
+
+The full package includes the EXE, all source/assets and the small compiled touch
+helper. Existing BlueStacks HD-Adb.exe is reused; no APK, root, Java or Android SDK
+installation is needed on your PC. `android_touch/` contains the Java source,
+build manifest and reproducible build instructions. Existing histories, Obtained
+choices, routes, counters, Endless, collection/return and heatmaps are retained.
+
+Windows validation uses an independent simulated Android subprocess and real Tk
+windows. It verifies screenshots, held gestures, map pan/restore, cancellation,
+saved settings and unchanged Windows cursor/foreground. The actual Java helper
+is also executed against Android API stubs and rebuilt from pinned tools. These
+checks do not prove live BlueStacks permissions or minimized rendering: run the
+included pan test on your PC.
+
